          "date": "2026-10-11 16:00:59.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20834 tests: show why a remote Lustre mount got ENODEV",
        "message": "LU-20834 tests: show why a remote Lustre mount got ENODEV\n\nWith LOAD_MODULES_REMOTE=false, remote servers and clients\nget their Lustre modules only from the kernel's fs-type\nautoload when mount_facet() or zconf_mount_clients() mounts\nthem. That autoload runs \"modprobe -q\", so a failed load\nleaves nothing but ENODEV and \"Are the lustre modules\nloaded?\", and setup stops, which Autotest reports as \"auster\nexited unexpectedly\". This hits RHEL 10.1 test nodes about\nonce in 1400 sessions, at a random module of the chain, and\nthe retest passes.\n\nOn ENODEV, load the modules for that fs type with\n\"modprobe -v\", which shows what it inserts and why it fails,\nand mount once more.\n\nTest-Parameters: fortestonly trivial testlist=sanity serverdistro=el10.1\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: patrick bot <patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us>\nChange-Id: I78b0d21d74123cf6a79257582757cd796375ea1f\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
